$\begin{align}
\text{vertex's }r\text{-coordinate}&=\dfrac{(\goldD{-10})+(\goldD{6})}{2}
\\\\
&=\blueD{-2}
\end{align}$

Now we can find the vertex's $y$-coordinate by evaluating $f(\blueD{-2})$:

$\begin{align}
f(\blueD{-2})&=(\blueD{-2})^2+4(\blueD{-2})-60
\\\\
&=4-8-60
\\\\
&=-64
\end{align}$
